<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neferkauhor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 22nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neferkauhor was a king of the Eighth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> who reigned briefly at Memphis late in the 22nd century BCE. He is known mainly from a series of decrees found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coptos">Coptos</a>, which grant offices and honours to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> Shemay and his son Idy. The decrees show the power of provincial families as the monarchy of the late Old Kingdom declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neferkauhor.jpg" alt="Neferkauhor" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ochmann-HH derivative work: Khruner · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abydos_KL_07-16_n55.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
